[Music]  i'm the first person to both fly in  space  and touch the deepest point in the ocean  [Music]  my missions have taken me over 2 million  feet above sea level  [Applause]  and 35 853 feet below sea level  i've seen things no other human being  has and they've absolutely changed me  in a lot of ways  [Music]  i'm kathy sullivan i'm an oceanographer  and astronaut  my interest in science showed up at very  early age  i really had a lust for adventure and  travel and exploration  my first space flight was in october of  1984  after 15 years as an astronaut i made my  way back to earth to focus on the oceans  i've always thought that it's too bad we  never created a nasa for the deepest  deepest parts of the sea  we know more about our moon and mars  than we do about the deep sea so little  is known about the shape of the bottom  so one of the objectives was mapping the  deep sea floor  [Music]  deep sea submersible dives and space  shuttle flights can be  pretty different  on the space shuttle took us eight and a  half minutes to go from zero miles an  hour to orbital velocity  17 500 miles an hour  it amounts to riding a bomb when you get  into orbit  you're a couple hundred miles above the  earth any direction you look  you can see probably nearly a thousand  miles  you get 16 sunrises and 16 sunsets in  every 24-hour day  you're just stunned by the number of  stars that you can see so  there kind of isn't really an inky black  of space that's anything like the  the inky black of the deep sea  going to the bottom of the ocean  contrast was like the world's  smoothest calmest elevator ride and it  took us  four hours to go from the surface to  nearly 36 000 feet  it is kind of like a magic school bus i  mean you're sitting inside this cozy  little metal sphere  you might be munching a tuna fish  sandwich and yet  outside that sphere pressure's about  1100 times  greater than it is here on the surface  of the earth  it's pitch dark except for what light  you bring with you on the submarine  we could maybe see 30 feet in whatever  direction we were looking at the  viewport  it was like a moonscape or an underwater  desert  it really is in a lot of ways harder to  explore and understand the ocean  i've spent a fair amount of time living  in these complex machines  i think intense experiences deepen the  value that you put on family on home so  i look back at my life  and i see vastly more blessings and  sacrifice  to actually have those experiences and  to deepen our understanding of our  planet and how many ways we depend on  that to me is all blessing  we are all sharing this one home this  one little spaceship earth  we have to look at it as a place that  you cherish in a place you want to  protect  we're on it together and we're  intimately connected  [Music]  hey everybody my name is drew bebe and  i'm here in my terrible  home studio that i've made during  quarantine  and i wanted to tell you about our new  podcast called great big story  it's got more surprising and delightful  stories just like this one  so head over to apple podcast to spotify  wherever you get your favorite podcasts  and download  great big story

